c Graph H_7 of Theorem 1 in 'The CLIQUES Algorithm Is Not Output-Polynomial' (Sec. 3)
c target n = 150; nearest H_k has n = 2k^2+9k = 161 vertices (k = 7)
c maximal cliques: 1121 (Lemma bound (k+1)(2k(k+3)+1) = 1128 <= n^2 = 25921)
c every run of CLIQUES makes at least 2^(k+1)-1 = 255 recursive calls (one run with min-label tie-breaking and increasing order: 7923)
c vertices: guards g_i = 1..7; core a_i = k+2i-1, b_i = k+2i (8..21); witnesses 22..161, 10 per core vertex in the order a_1, b_1, a_2, ...
p edge 161 2975
